# Utilities slice 4 — a District with no plant buys its Power at an Outside Connection.
#
#   godot --path src/Borough.Godot -- --load plans/evidence/utilities-slice-1/ridge.borough \
#     --drive plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/import.drive
#
# The world is slice 1's ridge, opened on Day 2 and fully delivered: a plant in the west District,
# an occupied dwelling in the east, and one Street crossing the boundary. The east District has no
# plant of its own, so cutting that Street leaves it with nothing. An Outside Connection raised in
# the east is then its only supply, and the treasury buys the Day.
#
# ⚠ THE RIDGE HAS NO VACANT LOT, so a filler dwelling is demolished to free one. All 44 of its Lots
# are built on and a gate stands on a vacant edge Lot. Lot 44 at east 253 is in the east District's
# Cell 7, on the south edge, and the south Hinterland is the one that prices Power.
#
# ⚠ ONE `shoot` PER TICK, AND THE CAMERA MOVES ON THE TICK IT SHOOTS. `_pendingShot` holds one path
# and the picture is taken on the NEXT frame, so a second `shoot` on the same Tick throws the first
# away and a camera moved after a `shoot` lands in that shot. Hence the gaps.
4097 pause
4097 overlay utilities
4097 ui building 37
4097 ui section utilities on
4097 ui section attention on
4097 turn left
4097 tilt 40
4097 focus 128 2 560
4097 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/01-day2-linked.png
4097 speed 8

# The trigger: the one crossing Street goes, and the east District is left with no plant, no
# neighbor and no gate. Day 2's fraction was fixed by the settle at Tick 4,096, so the reading does
# not move until the next one.
4101 pause
4101 hold street
4101 click 191 0 shift
4101 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/02-crossing-cut.png
4101 speed 8

# The settle at Tick 6,144 reads a road graph with no crossing and no import source. The east
# delivers nothing.
6150 pause
6150 hold look
6150 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/03-day3-short.png
6150 speed 8

# The response: clear a filler dwelling's Lot in Cell 7 and open an Outside Connection on it.
6152 pause
6152 hold demolish
6152 click 253 0
6152 speed 8
6154 pause
6154 hold gate
6154 click 253 0
6154 speed 8
6156 pause
6156 hold look
6156 tilt 45
6156 focus 240 3 120
6156 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/04-gate-raised.png
6156 speed 8

# The settle at Tick 8,192 finds the gate, buys the whole shortfall and pays for it. Day 4 runs at
# 100% on imported Power: 512 units of demand and 64 Tiles of road loss, bought gross at 2 each.
8200 pause
8200 tilt 40
8200 focus 128 2 560
8200 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/05-day4-imported.png
8200 speed 8
8202 pause
8202 tilt 45
8202 focus 240 3 120
8202 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/06-day4-imported-close.png
8202 speed 8

# The city budget. A Control is invisible to a caption, so the panel's own text comes from `ui read`
# beside the picture. ⚠ The inspector is closed first: it is anchored over the budget panel's figure
# columns and hides them.
8204 pause
8204 ui close
8204 ui budget on
8204 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/07-day4-budget.png
8204 ui read plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/07-day4-budget.json
8204 speed 8

# The settle at Tick 10,240 buys the same Day again. The bill recurs and the treasury keeps falling.
10248 pause
10248 shoot plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/08-day5-budget.png
10248 ui read plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/08-day5-budget.json
10248 speed 8

# The end state, saved through the menu.
#
# ⚠ THE WINDOW IS FIXED FIRST, because the picker's Save button is pressed at a coordinate and the
# dialog is centered on the viewport. ⚠ The menu stops the clock, so nothing may need a later Tick
# after this point. ⚠ `ui file-path` resolves a relative path against the GODOT PROJECT directory,
# unlike `shoot` and `readout`, which resolve against the repository root.
10250 pause
10250 ui size 1440 960
10250 ui menu on
10250 ui menu save
10250 ui file-path ../../plans/evidence/utilities-slice-4/importing.borough-city
10250 ui press 314 769
10250 quit
